From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] use schedule(static) for dist2holes's dynamic OpenMP loops

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [works around a libgomp defect on the riscv64 runners, riseproject-dev/python-wheels#617]

CI's cp313 leg segfaulted with "Fatal Python error: Segmentation
fault" in test_dist2holes.py::test_dist2holes_no_hole_filter, at the
line calling hp.dist2holes(mask) (PR #2430, run 36412601673, job
108896142667, head sha e9bbe3baf5). This is a different crash than the
one 0002 already fixes: same commit, different test and different
function, so 0002's libsharp loops are not involved here.

hp.dist2holes (src/_masktools.pyx) calls straight into
cextern/healpix's Healpix_cxx dist2holes() (mask_tools.cc), which
contains two OpenMP loops using non-static schedules: the border-pixel
scan (schedule(dynamic,10000)) and the final per-pixel distance walk
(schedule(dynamic)). Because the input mask here is RING-ordered,
dist2holes() also calls Healpix_Map::swap_scheme() (healpix_map.h) on
its way out, which has its own schedule(dynamic,1) loop. All three run
on every dist2holes() call with a RING mask, matching gotcha 166's
signature exactly: a fault inside the OpenMP runtime on the riscv64
runners' libgomp, specific to the dynamic/guided work-share schedules,
regardless of loop size.

Moving these three loops to schedule(static) costs load balancing,
not correctness. Tag it Inappropriate and revert once the runners'
toolchain is fixed, per gotcha 166.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 cextern/healpix/src/cxx/Healpix_cxx/healpix_map.h | 2 +-
 cextern/healpix/src/cxx/Healpix_cxx/mask_tools.cc | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/cextern/healpix/src/cxx/Healpix_cxx/healpix_map.h b/cextern/healpix/src/cxx/Healpix_cxx/healpix_map.h
index 126fdf8..79d63c7 100644
--- a/cextern/healpix/src/cxx/Healpix_cxx/healpix_map.h
+++ b/cextern/healpix/src/cxx/Healpix_cxx/healpix_map.h
@@ -183,7 +183,7 @@ template<typename T> class Healpix_Map: public Healpix_Base
 
       arr<int> cycle=swap_cycles();
 
-#pragma omp parallel for schedule(dynamic,1)
+#pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)
       for (tsize m=0; m<cycle.size(); ++m)
         {
         int istart = cycle[m];
diff --git a/cextern/healpix/src/cxx/Healpix_cxx/mask_tools.cc b/cextern/healpix/src/cxx/Healpix_cxx/mask_tools.cc
index 9756a50..093076e 100644
--- a/cextern/healpix/src/cxx/Healpix_cxx/mask_tools.cc
+++ b/cextern/healpix/src/cxx/Healpix_cxx/mask_tools.cc
@@ -75,7 +75,7 @@ Healpix_Map<double> dist2holes(const Healpix_Map<double> &mask, double maxdist)
     for (int i=0; i<mask.Npix(); ++i)
       maxmask[i] = (mask[i]==0) ? FULLY_IN_MASK : 0;
   // find border pixels
-#pragma omp parallel for schedule(dynamic,10000)
+#pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)
   for (int i=0; i<mask.Npix(); ++i)
     if (maxmask[i])
       {
@@ -163,7 +163,7 @@ Healpix_Map<double> dist2holes(const Healpix_Map<double> &mask, double maxdist)
       submask.push_back(i);
       subvec.push_back(omask[0].pix2vec(i));
       }
-#pragma omp parallel for schedule(dynamic)
+#pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)
   for (int i=0; i<omask[0].Npix(); ++i)
     process(0, i, submask, subvec);
 
